    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0213" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB/10–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-03T17:30:00-05:00">October 3, 1949—5:30
                        p. m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p> Delga 52. Following are decisions taken at GADel meeting today:</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>3. China. Delegation accepted Amb. Jessup’s suggestion that, in view of
                    proclamation of new Chinese “government” and its immediate recognition by USSR,
                    members of USDel, in discussing Chinese item, indicate this not unexpected and
                    does not change present situation, pointing out virtually automatic Soviet
                    recognition appears lend some color to Chinese charges of Soviet collusion and
                    support for puppet regime.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
